# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Binaries never belong in the repo; builds are reproducible from
# source (and never need the network).
bin/
/lotusui
cmd/lotusui/lotusui
*.exe
*.wasm

# ── Test & profiling artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────
*.test
*.coverprofile
coverage.*
*.prof
*.pprof

# ── Local Go workspace files ────────────────────────────────────────
# go.work is a per-machine dev convenience (e.g. linking the consumer
# apps); committing it would leak local paths into every checkout.
go.work
go.work.sum

# ── Docs site build output ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Also ignored by site/.gitignore; repeated here so tooling run from
# the root can't accidentally stage it. CI builds and deploys dist/;
# the repo holds sources only.
site/dist/

# ── Upstream reference checkouts (local only) ───────────────────────
# Agents clone shadcn/ui (and optionally chakra) here to read REAL
# example sources — never commit these trees.
_ref/

# ── Editor & OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ── Deliberately NOT ignored (doctrine) ─────────────────────────────
# assets/icons/*.svg + manifest — fetched at dev time, committed.
# site/looks/fonts/*.ttf         — fetched at dev time, committed.
# site/goldens/*.png             — golden screenshots, reviewed like code.
# *_gen.go, scales_gen.go        — generated AND committed; `lotusui
#                                  verify` keeps them honest in CI.
